---
// The same rewritten commit as git log shows it and as GitHub's push record
// shows it, side by side. An illustration with made-up IDs and times; the
// threat page says so.
---

<figure class="compare not-prose">
  <div class="side">
    <p class="label">What <code>git log</code> shows you</p>
    <pre>a41c9e2  Fix navbar spacing
         You · 12 Oct, 10:42</pre>
    <p class="verdict ok">Looks normal: your name, your message, the old date.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="side">
    <p class="label">What GitHub's push record shows</p>
    <pre>force-pushed main
from 7d03b18 to a41c9e2
by your account · 3 Nov, 02:13</pre>
    <p class="verdict bad">The real push: when it happened and that it replaced a commit.</p>
  </div>
  <figcaption>An example, with made-up commit IDs and times.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .compare {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .compare {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  .side {
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--pr-border);
    border-radius: var(--pr-radius);
    background: var(--pr-surface);
  }
  .label {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    color: var(--pr-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--pr-border);
    border-radius: var(--pr-radius-sm);
    background: var(--pr-bg);
    color: var(--pr-heading);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  .verdict {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .ok {
    color: var(--pr-text);
  }
  .bad {
    color: var(--pr-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  figcaption {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    color: var(--pr-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
  }
</style>
